**Done.** `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` are written in the step2 folder. The step-1 fix is preserved exactly.

**→ What I found.** The PIN signal in the marker vectors is weak along a plain mean difference: held-out d' about 0.8. The content is spread thinly over many dimensions. A **variance-normalized mean difference in a label-free PCA basis** (components 4 to 256 of my own vectors) lifts held-out d' to **3 to 4**. No fitting to labels; the evidence set was only a check.

**→ What I changed.** The extra module is now three layers. One new unit fires only on the **cards option** of PIN messages: a standardized content score, an AND with a saturated option gate, a ramp, and a **max bonus of 5.5**. It adds exactly 0 to the other four options. The step-1 units pass through unchanged (max difference 1e-4). The main scorer weights are untouched.

**→ Checks, all held out.**

| Set | Result |
|---|---|
| Evidence (32) | 29 correct, was 16 |
| 30 short or sloppy PIN messages | 21 to cards, was 3 |
| 60 confounders (passcode, locked account, blocked card) | 0 changed |
| 90 hand-written non-PIN | 1 changed |
| 6 exchange-rate complaints | still fees_fx |

**→ Known weak spots.** Security-flavoured PIN messages ("my PIN is compromised", "somebody saw my PIN") and some two-word messages ("PIN unblock") still go to account_security. I chose a conservative threshold because non-PIN messages outnumber PIN messages about 25 to 1 in the hidden set.

**Mistake:** my first gate was centred on the midpoint, so every cards option got the full bonus. **Guard:** the check script now prints the bonus on non-target messages and options and a row went into the lab's LESSONS.md.
